A Rust port of Emotecraft by KosmX and dima_dencep (https://github.com/KosmX/emotes,
branch dev, version 3.5.0 for Minecraft 26.3, commit a786648), for Horizon, the Rust
rewrite of Minecraft Java Edition 26.3. Emotecraft is under the GNU General Public
License version 3; this port is under the GNU General Public License version 3 only
(LICENSE). This port is not made, endorsed or supported by KosmX, dima_dencep, Mojang
or Microsoft. Report problems with the port at
https://github.com/DeportedToHell/MCRE-Mods/issues, not to Emotecraft's authors.


Statement of changes (GPL-3.0 section 5a)
-----------------------------------------
2026-11-11, DeportedToHell: Emotecraft's client and server (the Fabric/NeoForge mod
and the Paper plugin) rewritten in Rust as one Horizon native mod: the emote
player, the emote wheel and every screen drawn with Horizon's GUI, the network
protocol (emotecraft:emote and emotecraft:stream, every packet version), the
server's commands, the emote file formats, Opus songs played through the mod's own
audio output. Online Emotes and the cloud library are left out (their buttons stay
as Emotecraft shows them when the service is unavailable); the Geyser support is
left out. A Russian name for "Let's Groove" was added (Emotecraft's ru_RU has none).
While the mod is on, Horizon's own emote wheel key (B) opens Emotecraft's wheel.


From Emotecraft, unchanged
--------------------------
- the built-in emotes, their icons and songs, in mixins/emotecraft/data/emotes/
  (emotesAssets/src/main/resources/assets/emotecraft/emotes/);
- the mod logo (mixins/emotecraft/data/icon.png) and the folder icons
  (folder.png, folder_open.png);
- the English and Russian texts (assets/emotecraft/lang/en_us.json, ru_ru.json),
  in mixins/emotecraft/engine/src/lang.rs.

Built-in emotes by KosmX (Waving, Clap, Crying, Point, Over here, Face palm),
Kale Ko (Back Flip), Wah0o (Kazotsky kick, Roblox potion dance), 3APA3EH (Club
penguin, Twerk, Let's Groove) and SPEmotes (Caramell Dance, Take the L), as
Emotecraft credits them. The three songs (Caramelldansen, Let's Groove, Take the L)
come with Emotecraft's built-in emotes as Emotecraft ships them; their rights
belong to their owners. Deleting their entries from mixins/emotecraft/songs.rs and
the .opus files removes them.

The translations are Emotecraft's own, made by its translators on Crowdin
(https://crowdin.com/project/emotecraft, project 414868).


Libraries the port is based on
------------------------------
Emotecraft plays emotes with PlayerAnimationLibrary by ZigyTheBird
(https://github.com/ZigyTheBird/PlayerAnimationLibrary), which is based on
GeckoLib 4.8.4 (commit 2d7dc6e) and on playerAnimator by KosmX, and uses
mochafloats (Molang) by Unnamed Team. Their animation logic (the controller, the
keyframes and easings, the Bedrock and PlayerAnimator loaders, the binary format)
and the Molang parser and interpreter are rewritten in Rust in
